LEGAL NOTICE
(Under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 — Pre-Complaint Notice)

To,
{respondent}
{respondentAddress}

From,
{applicant}
Through: {advocateName}, Advocate
{advocateAddress}

prayerTemplate:
You are hereby called upon to, within 30 (thirty) days of receipt of this notice:
(a) {primary_relief — e.g., REFUND the entire consideration of Rs. {amount}/- paid by my client / REPLACE the defective goods with a new defect-free product / REPAIR the said goods free of cost to my client's satisfaction / REMOVE the deficiency in service complained of};
(b) Pay compensation in the sum of Rs. {compensation_amount}/- towards mental agony, harassment, loss of time, and consequential losses suffered by my client on account of your deficiency in service / defect in goods / unfair trade practice;
(c) Pay interest at the rate of {interest_rate}% per annum on Rs. {amount}/- from {date_of_payment} until realisation;
(d) Reimburse litigation costs and the cost of this notice in the sum of Rs. {notice_cost}/-.

Failing the above, my client shall be constrained to file a Consumer Complaint against you under Section 35 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 before the competent {forum} (having pecuniary jurisdiction over claims of Rs. {total_value}/-, in accordance with the Consumer Protection (Jurisdiction of the District Commission, the State Commission and the National Commission) Rules, 2021), seeking the above reliefs along with such other reliefs as the Commission may deem fit, entirely at your risk, cost, and consequences.

PLEASE TAKE FURTHER NOTICE that my client also reserves the right to file a complaint with the Central Consumer Protection Authority (CCPA) for unfair trade practice / misleading advertisement under Sections 17-19 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, and to claim product liability under Sections 82-87 thereof.
